rows=[
(0,None,'b00014',q1,'Frontal abdominal radiograph with two arrows.','A single grayscale frontal abdominal projection shows a central bright vertebral column, lower ribs, pelvis and bowel gas outlines. Two broad white arrows point down and toward small bright spots on opposite sides of the lumbar spine. An unlabeled horizontal ticked bar lies at the bottom. An outlined square containing 4 is at lower right; it is an acquisition marker of uncertain meaning, not a separately labelled panel. No legible units, numerical dimensions or date appear.','x_ray','erect abdominal radiograph',[('kidneys','both kidneys')],'The caption identifies small high-density lesions in both kidneys; the case text treats this as the initial radiograph in the renal-stone workup.',['The bottom tick bar has no readable physical calibration; stone sizes cannot be measured from pixels.']),
(1,'A','b00015',q2a,'Axial pelvic CT view with an arrow beside the bladder.','The left image is an axial pelvic cross-section on black. A rounded gray central region lies between bright bony structures. A white arrow slopes down-left toward a small dense white spot beside that central region on image left. A circled A labels the lower-left corner. No laterality label, caliper, scale, dimension or date is printed.','ct','non-contrast CT; axial view',[('right distal ureter','right distal ureter')],'The caption identifies a right distal ureteral high-density lesion and reports 0.5×0.8 cm. The measurement and anatomical laterality are caption claims; no visible caliper supports an independent pixel measurement.',[]),
(1,'B','b00015',q2bc,'Coronal CT view with an arrow toward dense renal spots on image left.','The middle image is a coronal abdominal/pelvic cross-section with bright vertebral bodies and pelvic bones. A white arrow points down-right into several tiny bright spots within a kidney-shaped region on image left. Gray soft tissues and dark bowel spaces surround the spine. A circled B labels the lower left. No printed dimension, scale, side marker or date is visible.','ct','non-contrast CT; coronal view',[('renal calyces','renal calyces')],'The shared B/C caption describes multiple renal calyceal high-density lesions up to 0.5×0.6 cm and accompanying mild hydronephrosis. It does not independently assign the dimensional maximum or hydronephrosis to a particular B/C side.',['B and C share one source caption clause; panel-specific stone count, maximum measurement and hydronephrosis side are not established.']),
(1,'C','b00015',q2bc,'Coronal CT view with an arrow toward a small renal spot on image right.','The right image is a coronal abdominal/pelvic cross-section showing the bright spine and pelvis. A white arrow slopes down-left toward a small bright spot within a gray kidney-shaped region on image right. Large gray soft-tissue regions lie above, with dark bowel spaces lower centrally. A circled C labels the lower-left corner. No printed caliper, physical scale, laterality label or date appears.','ct','non-contrast CT; coronal view',[('renal calyces','renal calyces')],'The shared B/C caption describes multiple renal calyceal high-density lesions up to 0.5×0.6 cm and accompanying mild hydronephrosis. It does not independently assign the dimensional maximum or hydronephrosis to a particular B/C side.',['B and C share one source caption clause; panel-specific stone count, maximum measurement and hydronephrosis side are not established.']),
(2,'A','b00016',q3a,'Early scintigraphy projection with paired darker lower-neck regions.','The left grayscale planar projection has diffuse mottled darker areas in the upper face/head and paired dark rounded regions near the lower neck. An R marker is printed at the far left, and a circled A at lower left. No arrow, acquisition clock, tracer dose, pixel calibration or numerical uptake value is printed.','nuclear_medicine','Tc-99m MIBI parathyroid scintigraphy',[('thyroid glands','both thyroid glands')],'The caption identifies the 15-minute scan phase and increased uptake in both thyroid glands. The timing and gland labels come from text, rather than printed pixel time or quantitative uptake.',['No numerical uptake or tracer dose/route is supplied; caption timing is relative with unspecified time-zero.']),
(2,'B','b00016',q3b,'Delayed scintigraphy projection with an arrow to a small lower-neck focus.','The right grayscale planar projection has diffuse mottled darker face/head regions. A black arrow slopes down-right toward a small focal dark spot near the lower central neck on image left. An L marker appears at the far right, and a circled B labels the lower left. No 2-hour clock, tracer dose, quantitative uptake or dimensional calibration is printed.','nuclear_medicine','Tc-99m MIBI parathyroid scintigraphy',[('anterior right thyroid gland','anterior portion (arrow) of the right thyroid gland')],'The caption identifies the 2-hour phase and retained uptake only anterior to the right thyroid. The body reports localization of a parathyroid mass there; no adenoma histology or malignancy is inferred from this scan.',['Anatomical laterality and retained uptake are author claims. No quantitative uptake or histology follows from pixel appearance.'])]
for idx,fm in enumerate(m['figures']):
 pp=[];aa=[];sid='b00014' if idx==0 else 'b00015' if idx==1 else 'b00016'
 callout='An initial erect abdominal radiograph revealed tiny high-density lesions in both kidneys (Fig. 1).' if idx==0 else 'Computed tomography of the kidney and bladder revealed a stone measuring 0.5×0.8 cm in the right distal ureter with hydronephrosis as well as multiple small calyceal stones in both kidneys (up to 0.5×0.6 cm) (Fig. 2).' if idx==1 else 'Technetium-99m sestamibi parathyroid scintigraphy identified a parathyroid mass at the anterior portion of the right thyroid gland (Fig. 3).'
 for i,c,sid,q,g,d,mod,sub,bodies,sig,lim in rows:
  if i!=idx:continue
